---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pageTitle = "Terms of Service | Lakeland Repair";
const pageDescription = "Terms of service, repair service policies, warranty coverage, and payment terms for Lakeland Repair.";
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  
  <!-- Custom Legal Hero -->
  <section class="relative bg-brand-teal text-white overflow-hidden py-16 lg:py-24 border-b border-teal-800">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top_right,_var(--tw-gradient-stops))] from-teal-700/40 via-brand-teal-dark to-brand-teal-dark z-0"></div>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-teal-800/80 border border-teal-600/50 text-teal-100 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase mb-6">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-amber" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/></svg>
        <span>Legal Documentation</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-heading font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-4">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-teal-100/80 text-sm">Last Updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-brand-surface">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl shadow-xl border border-gray-100 p-8 sm:p-12 lg:p-16">
        
        <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-600 marker:text-brand-teal">
          
          <div class="bg-brand-teal/5 border-l-4 border-brand-teal p-6 rounded-r-2xl mb-12">
            <p class="m-0 font-medium text-brand-teal-dark">
              Please review these Terms of Service prior to scheduling repair services. These terms outline the service agreement between you (the customer) and Lakeland Repair.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">1. Scope of Repair Services</h2>
          <p>
            Lakeland Repair provides professional residential and light commercial appliance diagnostic and repair services across Lakeland and surrounding Polk County, Florida communities. All repairs require customer authorization following an in-person diagnostic evaluation and upfront flat-rate price quote.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">2. Diagnostics & Upfront Pricing</h2>
          <p>
            A standard diagnostic service fee covers the technician's travel, specialized troubleshooting, and testing to accurately identify equipment failures. When a customer approves the recommended repair during the initial diagnostic visit, the diagnostic fee is credited directly toward the final invoice total.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">3. 90-Day Parts & Labor Warranty</h2>
          <p>
            Completed repairs include a 90-day limited warranty on newly installed OEM factory parts and associated repair labor. If the identical component fails within 90 days of the repair date, we will replace the part and correct the issue at no additional labor cost.
          </p>
          <p>The warranty does not cover:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Subsequent, unrelated component or electrical failures.</li>
            <li>Power surges, lightning strikes, or external plumbing issues.</li>
            <li>Physical damage, customer misuse, or unauthorized tampering.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">4. Payment Terms</h2>
          <p>
            Payment is due upon completion of the authorized repair service. We accept major credit cards (Visa, MasterCard, Discover, American Express), debit cards, cash, and company checks. Itemized digital receipts are provided upon receipt of payment.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">5. Appointments & Access</h2>
          <p>
            Customers are responsible for ensuring an adult (18 years or older) is present during the scheduled service window and that the appliance is safely accessible to the technician with necessary water, gas, or electrical shut-offs available.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">6. Governing Law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Florida. Any legal action or proceeding arising under these terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Polk County, Florida.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-brand-teal-dark mt-10 mb-4 border-b border-gray-100 pb-4">7. Contact Information</h2>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 mt-6">
            <p class="m-0 text-sm">
              If you have any questions regarding our service policies, please contact our dispatch desk:<br><br>
              <strong>Lakeland Repair</strong><br>
              120 E Pine St, Suite 4<br>
              Lakeland, FL 33801<br>
              Phone: <a href="tel:+18632780714" class="text-brand-amber font-bold hover:underline">(863) 278-0714</a>
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
